WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.330
Ammonia plants make ammonia
from nitrogen and hydrogen.

2
00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:09.450
Inside, they squeeze the gases to
about 200 times atmospheric pressure.

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.790
Holding gases at that
pressure is a lot of trouble.

4
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.170
So why go to all that effort?

5
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:20.770
Why do ammonia plants squeeze their gases
to about 200 times atmospheric pressure?

6
00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.490
In this mission, you'll meet
Le Châtelier's principle,

7
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:27.210
and use it to predict what happens
when you disturb an equilibrium.

8
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.650
You'll change concentrations,
pressure and temperature,

9
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:36.590
and see which changes move the position
of equilibrium, and which change K itself.

10
00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.910
Your mission: explain why ammonia
plants run at such high pressure.
